From 8d2885fc2408fb9a65d82843b0702141c945f084 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:29:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-29: rubber-band selection, zoom to fit, the Visual
 Studio keys F4 / Ctrl+Alt+X / Ctrl+Alt+T (0.29.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Rubber band (WPF): a drag that starts on the form's own background -- or
  outside the form -- draws a dashed band; on release the components entirely
  inside it become the selection, the outermost only (a panel and its
  children both inside: the panel); design-hidden ones do not count.
  (The probe's mouseup handler now ends a band too -- it stops the event for
  the page, so the window's own mouseup listener never runs.)
- 縮放到符合視窗 (title bar, right-click): the largest zoom step at which the
  whole form fits the view, measured in the form's own px.
- F4 = the properties panel, Ctrl+Alt+X = the toolbox, Ctrl+Alt+T = the
  component tree (document outline), while the designer is active.

Tests: probe (fit: 1.25 on HotPlate, 0.9 on Speed, the form fits; a band
from outside past the top-left corner: 8 / 9 components, all entirely
inside), smoke 95, real VS Code 97 (the real webview picks a step; the three
view commands exist), lib 121, panels -- all pass; NO-SAVES.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
